# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Seed optimization**: By default, `seed_transpiler` is `None`, and transpilation level 2 searches over transpiler seeds to find the circuit with the best depth. If you set a seed, the function skips that search and the transpilation is reproducible.\n"
msgstr "**Pengoptimuman seed**: Secara lalai, `seed_transpiler` ialah `None`, dan transpilasi tahap 2 mencari merentasi seed transpiler untuk mendapatkan litar dengan kedalaman terbaik. Jika anda menetapkan seed, fungsi melangkau carian itu dan transpilasi boleh diulang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Transpilation levels (1-3)**: The `transpilation_level` option selects the transpilation method.\n"
"- **Level 1**: Standard Qiskit transpiler.\n"
"- **Level 2** (default): Improved transpiler that searches over 15 transpiler seeds and keeps the best circuit. If you set `seed_transpiler`, the function skips the search.\n"
"- **Level 3**: Line routing with the swap strategy for a linear coupling map that is described in Section 2.2.1 of [Weidenfeller et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03459) Line routing follows a fixed swap schedule, so its circuit depth grows linearly with the number of variables. For densely connected problems, line routing typically produces shallower circuits than levels 1 and 2 and transpiles faster. Level 3 supports at most 127 variables on Heron r2 and r3 processors, 112 variables on Heron r1, and 120 variables on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Tahap transpilasi (1-3)**: Pilihan `transpilation_level` memilih kaedah transpilasi.\n"
"- **Tahap 1**: Transpiler Qiskit standard.\n"
"- **Tahap 2** (lalai): Transpiler yang dipertingkat yang mencari merentasi 15 seed transpiler dan mengekalkan litar terbaik. Jika anda menetapkan `seed_transpiler`, fungsi melangkau carian itu.\n"
"- **Tahap 3**: Penghalaan garisan dengan strategi swap untuk peta gandingan linear yang diterangkan dalam Seksyen 2.2.1 [Weidenfeller et al.](https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03459) Penghalaan garisan mengikut jadual swap tetap, jadi kedalaman litarnya bertambah secara linear dengan bilangan pemboleh ubah. Untuk masalah yang berhubung padat, penghalaan garisan lazimnya menghasilkan litar yang lebih cetek daripada tahap 1 dan 2 dan mentranspil dengan lebih pantas. Tahap 3 menyokong paling banyak 127 pemboleh ubah pada pemproses Heron r2 dan r3, 112 pemboleh ubah pada Heron r1, dan 120 pemboleh ubah pada Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Version 3.0.0 removed levels 0, 4, and 5. A job that requests one of them fails with error `1221`.\n"
msgstr "Versi 3.0.0 membuang tahap 0, 4, dan 5. Job yang meminta salah satu daripadanya gagal dengan ralat `1221`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function sizes {#function-sizes}"
msgstr "Saiz fungsi {#function-sizes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every job runs at one size, `S`, `M`, or `L`. If the size is too small, the platform rejects the job. If the size is larger than the job needs, the job runs on a bigger compute profile than the work requires. See [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) for how sizes work in general.\n"
msgstr "Setiap job berjalan pada satu saiz, `S`, `M`, atau `L`. Jika saiz terlalu kecil, platform menolak job itu. Jika saiz lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan job, job berjalan pada profil pengiraan yang lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan oleh kerja itu. Lihat [Saiz fungsi](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) untuk cara saiz berfungsi secara umum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The size depends on two properties of your model, the number of variables and the interaction density. The interaction density is the fraction of all variable pairs that appear together in a term of the objective or of a constraint.\n"
msgstr "Saiz bergantung pada dua sifat model anda, iaitu bilangan pemboleh ubah dan ketumpatan interaksi. Ketumpatan interaksi ialah pecahan bagi semua pasangan pemboleh ubah yang muncul bersama dalam satu sebutan objektif atau kekangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Size | Variables and interaction density | Compute profile | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `S` | At most 50 variables and a density of at most 0.1 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | At most 100 variables and a density of at most 0.25 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
"| `L` | Any model above either `M` bound | `48x768` | 48 | 768 GB |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Saiz | Pemboleh ubah dan ketumpatan interaksi | Profil pengiraan | vCPU | RAM |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| `S` | Paling banyak 50 pemboleh ubah dan ketumpatan paling tinggi 0.1 | `8x32` | 8 | 32 GB |\n"
"| `M` | Paling banyak 100 pemboleh ubah dan ketumpatan paling tinggi 0.25 | `16x128` | 16 | 128 GB |\n"
"| `L` | Mana-mana model yang melebihi salah satu had `M` | `48x768` | 48 | 768 GB |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A model must fit both bounds of a size. For this reason, a small model with many interactions might need `L`. For example, 10 variables that are all coupled to each other have a density of 1.0. Every optimization function uses the same bounds, so a size means the same model difficulty in every function.\n"
msgstr "Sesuatu model mesti memenuhi kedua-dua had bagi sesuatu saiz. Oleh sebab itu, model kecil dengan banyak interaksi mungkin memerlukan `L`. Contohnya, 10 pemboleh ubah yang semuanya berpasangan antara satu sama lain mempunyai ketumpatan 1.0. Setiap fungsi pengoptimuman menggunakan had yang sama, jadi sesuatu saiz bermaksud tahap kesukaran model yang sama dalam setiap fungsi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two features of a model raise the density more than you might expect.\n"
msgstr "Dua ciri model menaikkan ketumpatan lebih daripada yang anda jangkakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A term over more than two variables couples every pair of them. For example, a term in four variables contributes all six pairs.\n"
msgstr "Sebutan ke atas lebih daripada dua pemboleh ubah memasangkan setiap pasangan antaranya. Contohnya, sebutan dalam empat pemboleh ubah menyumbang kesemua enam pasangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A constraint counts as the penalty that replaces it on hardware. The squared constraint couples every pair of variables in it, so a one-hot constraint over four variables also contributes all six pairs.\n"
msgstr "Kekangan dikira sebagai penalti yang menggantikannya pada perkakasan. Kekangan yang dikuadratkan memasangkan setiap pasangan pemboleh ubah di dalamnya, jadi kekangan satu-panas ke atas empat pemboleh ubah juga menyumbang kesemua enam pasangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If a job does not request a size, it runs at the default size, `M`.\n"
msgstr "Jika job tidak meminta saiz, ia berjalan pada saiz lalai, `M`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To read the sizes from the function itself, call `optimizer.sizes()`. To read the default size, call `optimizer.get_default_size()`.\n"
msgstr "Untuk membaca saiz daripada fungsi itu sendiri, panggil `optimizer.sizes()`. Untuk membaca saiz lalai, panggil `optimizer.get_default_size()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Calculate the size before you submit a job {#calculate-the-size-before-you-submit-a-job}"
msgstr "Kira saiz sebelum anda menyerahkan job {#calculate-the-size-before-you-submit-a-job}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The calculator reads your model and nothing else. It submits no job and reserves nothing, so you can call it as often as you need while you reduce a model to a smaller size.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulator hanya membaca model anda dan tiada yang lain. Ia tidak menyerahkan job dan tidak menempah apa-apa, jadi anda boleh memanggilnya sekerap yang diperlukan semasa anda mengecilkan model kepada saiz yang lebih kecil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The calculator requires the `qiskit-addon-opt-mapper` package. To install it, run the following command.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulator memerlukan pakej `qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`. Untuk memasangnya, jalankan arahan berikut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size a sparse problem {#size-a-sparse-problem}"
msgstr "Tentukan saiz masalah jarang {#size-a-sparse-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a ring of 40 spins, where each spin interacts only with its two neighbors. The ring has 40 interacting pairs out of 780, which is a density of about 0.05, so it fits both bounds of `S`.\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan gelang 40 spin, di mana setiap spin hanya berinteraksi dengan dua jirannya. Gelang ini mempunyai 40 pasangan berinteraksi daripada 780, iaitu ketumpatan lebih kurang 0.05, jadi ia memenuhi kedua-dua had `S`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output is `S`. Pass the result to `run`.\n"
msgstr "Outputnya ialah `S`. Hantar hasilnya kepada `run`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the size is too small, the job fails with error `4600`, and the error message names the size to use. If the size is larger than the job needs, the job runs normally and records a `4601` advisory event. See [Function sizes](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) to learn more.\n"
msgstr "Jika saiz terlalu kecil, job gagal dengan ralat `4600`, dan mesej ralat menamakan saiz yang perlu digunakan. Jika saiz lebih besar daripada yang diperlukan job, job berjalan seperti biasa dan merekodkan peristiwa nasihat `4601`. Lihat [Saiz fungsi](/guides/managed-workflow-compute-profiles#best-practice-match-sizes-to-problem-sizes) untuk mengetahui lebih lanjut.\n"

